        interpretation: "This derives the slab formula from a constitutive gradient law plus steady energy conservation; it is not a universal consequence of conservation alone. Boundary temperatures belong to the slab surfaces, not automatically to surrounding room air. Thermal bridges and side losses break the one-dimensional model.",
